30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems usage is heavily skewed toward those sitting nearest the door, and eating at desks is creating a mess.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our social cohesion is lacking. We have no private space for difficult talks, and unplanned chat is limited to the printer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"A hot lunch takes twenty-five minutes round trip, and the old fridge was a disaster of abandoned food.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We spent 68,000 yen on small outside rentals last year. A meeting fit-out is 141,000, while a kitchen is 96,000.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The wall is mere plasterboard; everything is audible. Interestingly, the store room has had zero facilities issues.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the outside hire cost suggests a need for a meeting space, but the desk crumbs suggest a need for a kitchen.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"A meeting space could solve the ""awkward conversation"" problem if it provides actual privacy.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"If we have a kitchen, we save time on lunch trips, but Ryuji's point about the mess is valid.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"The meeting space is more expensive to install, but it stops the monthly bleed of outside hire fees.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"If we make it a kitchen, the noise and smells will penetrate that thin wall and disturb everyone.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A quiet room would solve the noise issue, but it doesn't address the financial loss or the lunch efficiency.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A quiet room is for individuals. We need a place for the ""us"" that we've forgotten how to be.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, is a meeting room any quieter than a kitchen?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Probably not, unless we invest in the wall, which isn't in the quotes.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,A meeting room is for structured talk; a kitchen is for chaos. The wall cannot handle chaos.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We must weigh the utility of a kitchen against the professional necessity of a meeting space.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I lean toward a space that encourages connection, even if it's formal.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I'm torn. The time saved on lunch is a huge quality-of-life boost.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's be rational. The outside hire is a recurring cost. A meeting room is a one-time investment.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,I simply wish for the office area to remain a sanctuary of focus.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The options are an Open Kitchen, a Quiet Room, or a Meeting Space. I prioritize the professional need.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A Meeting Space allows for the private, necessary conversations we currently lack.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"The Open Kitchen is tempting for the convenience, but the cleaning history is worrying.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Meeting Space is the only option that makes financial sense in the long run.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A Quiet Room would be the most peaceful, but a Meeting Space is a fair compromise.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,I will vote for the Meeting Space. It is the most logical use of the area.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Ryuji. Meeting Space it is.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"If everyone is against the kitchen, I can't fight it. I'll go with Meeting Space too.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,I'm glad we're seeing sense. Meeting Space.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"I can support the Meeting Space, provided we keep the volume reasonable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
